    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's a potential script paragraph:\n\n\"The notion of 'gentle parenting' has led some to challenge the idea of parental authority, advocating for a more empathetic and accepting approach to discipline. However, this emphasis on avoiding conflict and criticism can have unintended consequences. By blurring the lines between parent and child, gentle parenting sidelines the natural development of authority structures, leading to a generation of children who struggle to respect rules, boundaries, and leadership. Without the acknowledgment of a authority figure, children fail to learn the distinction between obedience and submission, and instead begin to see authority as oppressive or arbitrary. As a result, they may grow into adults who have difficulty respecting institutions, authority figures, and social hierarchies – skills that are crucial for success in personal and professional life. By dismantling the concept of parental authority, gentle parenting risks creating a society of entitled, disobedient individuals who are unprepared to navigate the complexities of adulthood.\"",
